Chapter: CodexWasmHarness

 THE PLUG'S OWN ROAD, with a file for a wire. `codex/plugs/wasm/WasmPlug.codex`
 reads IR text off the serial line and emits; this reads the same IR text from
 stdin, so a corpus of `.ir` files can be swept without compiling anything.

 It carries no front end on purpose -- the point is to exercise the EMITTER
 over many programs, and the corpus already holds their IR. The front end is
 still bundled and simply prunes away unreachable, which is why the binary this
 builds is 577 KB of zig against the full transpiler's 2.4 MB.

 `corpus_sweep.py` is the only caller.

  opening : [Console, FileSystem] Nothing = act
    src <- read-file-uni "/dev/stdin"
    let parsed = parse-ir-chapter src
    in emit-wasm-chapter-stream (parsed.chapter) (parsed.type-defs)
  end
